<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Laguna, Santa Catarina</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Laguna is a coastal town in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santa-catarina">Santa Catarina</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, founded by Portuguese settlers in the 1670s. In July 1839 rebels of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ragamuffin-war">Ragamuffin War</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/davi-canabarro">Davi Canabarro</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi">Giuseppe Garibaldi</a> captured it and proclaimed the short-lived Juliana Republic there. It was the birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anita-garibaldi">Anita Garibaldi</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/laguna-santa-catarina.jpg" alt="Laguna, Santa Catarina" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wilson Schuelter · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Casario_do_Centro_Hist%C3%B3rico_de_Laguna.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
